  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "sshdump: fix remote-sudo parameter on restart",
  "description": "remote-sudo is set to ws_no_argument, and is treated like a flag,\n   where boolean parameters are ignored.\n\nBefore: extcap was treating remote-sudo as a boolean, passing in\n   '--remote-sudo false', which triggered sudo mode.\nNow: Setting remote-sudo to a 'boolflag' matches ws_no_argument, and\n   ensures that extcap doesn't pass in '--remote-sudo', when the sudo\n   option is not checked.\n\nThis would previously happen in this scenario:\n1. Configure \"SSH remote capture\"\n2. Double click to run in GUI (this works)\n3. Capture -> Restart (this didn't work)\n\nCloses https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/issues/16929",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2022-03-12T18:21:37.137Z",
